+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770736
+name: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy
+namespace: mondo
+def: "Any Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is characterized by intellectual disability, developmental delay, hypotonia, motor impairment, variable brain structural anomalies including pontocerebellar hypoplasia and ventriculomegaly, and in some affected individuals thrombotic microangiopathy with proteinuria, severe hypertension, and end-stage kidney disease." [PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:34964109, PMID:37338178]
+synonym: "pontocerebellar hypoplasia type 2B" RELATED [PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994]
